 ### Defocus Blur Modeling
-Models optical defocus by adjusting the scale $s$ of 3D Gaussians based on their distance from the camera's focal plane [S4]. During training, larger scale values $\hat{s}_j$ are used to rasterize blurred images; during testing, smaller scale values $s_j$ are used to render sharp details [S4]. Unlike a naive Gaussian kernel that blurs the entire image uniformly, this method selectively enlarges covariances only for Gaussians corresponding to blurred regions [S4].
+Defocus Blur Modeling models optical defocus by adjusting the scale $s$ of 3D Gaussians based on their distance from the camera's focal plane [S4]. During training, use larger scale values $\bar{s}_j$ to rasterize blurred images. During testing, use smaller scale values $s_j$ to render sharp details. The scale $s$ (scale of a 3D Gaussian) controls dispersion; larger $s$ models out-of-focus points, smaller $s$ models in-focus points. Unlike a naive Gaussian kernel that blurs the entire image uniformly, this method selectively enlarges covariances only for Gaussians corresponding to blurred regions [S4].
 
